#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:1
msgid ""
"ipaddr.js — an IPv6 and IPv4 address manipulation library [![Build "
"Status](https://travis-ci.org/whitequark/ipaddr.js.svg)](https://travis-"
"ci.org/whitequark/ipaddr.js)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:1
msgid "Build Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:3
msgid ""
"ipaddr.js is a small (1.9K minified and gzipped) library for manipulating"
" IP addresses in JavaScript environments. It runs on both CommonJS "
"runtimes (e.g. [nodejs]) and in a web browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:7
msgid ""
"ipaddr.js allows you to verify and parse string representation of an IP "
"address, match it against a CIDR range or range list, determine if it "
"falls into some reserved ranges (examples include loopback and private "
"ranges), and convert between IPv4 and IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:14
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:16
msgid "`npm install ipaddr.js`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:18 ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:213
#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:228
msgid "or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:20
msgid "`bower install ipaddr.js`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:22
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:24
msgid ""
"ipaddr.js defines one object in the global scope: `ipaddr`. In CommonJS, "
"it is exported from the module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:31
msgid ""
"The API consists of several global methods and two classes: ipaddr.IPv6 "
"and ipaddr.IPv4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:33
msgid "Global methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:35
msgid ""
"There are three global methods defined: `ipaddr.isValid`, `ipaddr.parse` "
"and `ipaddr.process`. All of them receive a string as a single parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:38
msgid ""
"The `ipaddr.isValid` method returns `true` if the address is a valid IPv4"
" or IPv6 address, and `false` otherwise. It does not throw any "
"exceptions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:41
msgid ""
"The `ipaddr.parse` method returns an object representing the IP address, "
"or throws an `Error` if the passed string is not a valid representation "
"of an IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:45
msgid ""
"The `ipaddr.process` method works just like the `ipaddr.parse` one, but "
"it automatically converts IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses to their IPv4 "
"counterparts before returning. It is useful when you have a Node.js "
"instance listening on an IPv6 socket, and the `net.ivp6.bindv6only` "
"sysctl parameter (or its equivalent on non-Linux OS) is set to 0. In this"
" case, you can accept IPv4 connections on your IPv6-only socket, but the "
"remote address will be mangled. Use `ipaddr.process` method to "
"automatically demangle it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:53
msgid "Object representation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:55
msgid ""
"Parsing methods return an object which descends from `ipaddr.IPv6` or "
"`ipaddr.IPv4`. These objects share some properties, but most of them "
"differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:58
msgid "Shared properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:60
msgid ""
"One can determine the type of address by calling `addr.kind()`. It will "
"return either `\"ipv6\"` or `\"ipv4\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:63
msgid ""
"An address can be converted back to its string representation with "
"`addr.toString()`. Note that this method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:65
msgid ""
"does not return the original string used to create the object (in fact, "
"there is no way of getting that string)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:67
msgid "returns a compact representation (when it is applicable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:69
msgid ""
"A `match(range, bits)` method can be used to check if the address falls "
"into a certain CIDR range. Note that an address can be (obviously) "
"matched only against an address of the same type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:73 ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:86
#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:139 ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:207
#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:222
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:82
msgid ""
"Alternatively, `match` can also be called as `match([range, bits])`. In "
"this way, it can be used together with the `parseCIDR(string)` method, "
"which parses an IP address together with a CIDR range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:94
msgid ""
"A `range()` method returns one of predefined names for several special "
"ranges defined by IP protocols. The exact names (and their respective "
"CIDR ranges) can be looked up in the source: [IPv6 ranges] and [IPv4 "
"ranges]. Some common ones include `\"unicast\"` (the default one) and "
"`\"reserved\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:99
msgid ""
"You can match against your own range list by using "
"`ipaddr.subnetMatch(address, rangeList, defaultName)` method. It can work"
" with a mix of IPv6 or IPv4 addresses, and accepts a name-to-subnet map "
"as the range list. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:113
msgid ""
"The addresses can be converted to their byte representation with "
"`toByteArray()`. (Actually, JavaScript mostly does not know about byte "
"buffers. They are emulated with arrays of numbers, each in range of "
"0..255.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:122
msgid ""
"The `ipaddr.IPv4` and `ipaddr.IPv6` objects have some methods defined, "
"too. All of them have the same interface for both protocols, and are "
"similar to global methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:125
msgid ""
"`ipaddr.IPvX.isValid(string)` can be used to check if the string is a "
"valid address for particular protocol, and `ipaddr.IPvX.parse(string)` is"
" the error-throwing parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:128
msgid ""
"`ipaddr.IPvX.isValid(string)` uses the same format for parsing as the "
"POSIX `inet_ntoa` function, which accepts unusual formats like "
"`0xc0.168.1.1` or `0x10000000`. The function "
"`ipaddr.IPv4.isValidFourPartDecimal(string)` validates the IPv4 address "
"and also ensures that it is written in four-part decimal format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:133
msgid "IPv6 properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:135
msgid ""
"Sometimes you will want to convert IPv6 not to a compact string "
"representation (with the `::` substitution); the `toNormalizedString()` "
"method will return an address where all zeroes are explicit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:147
msgid ""
"The `isIPv4MappedAddress()` method will return `true` if this address is "
"an IPv4-mapped one, and `toIPv4Address()` will return an IPv4 object "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:150
msgid ""
"To access the underlying binary representation of the address, use "
"`addr.parts`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:157
msgid "A IPv6 zone index can be accessed via `addr.zoneId`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:164
msgid "IPv4 properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:166
msgid ""
"`toIPv4MappedAddress()` will return a corresponding IPv4-mapped IPv6 "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:168
msgid "To access the underlying representation of the address, use `addr.octets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:175
msgid ""
"`prefixLengthFromSubnetMask()` will return a CIDR prefix length for a "
"valid IPv4 netmask or null if the netmask is not valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:183
msgid ""
"`subnetMaskFromPrefixLength()` will return an IPv4 netmask for a valid "
"CIDR prefix length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:190
msgid ""
"`broadcastAddressFromCIDR()` will return the broadcast address for a "
"given IPv4 interface and netmask in CIDR notation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:194
msgid ""
"`networkAddressFromCIDR()` will return the network address for a given "
"IPv4 interface and netmask in CIDR notation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:199
msgid "Conversion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:201
msgid ""
"IPv4 and IPv6 can be converted bidirectionally to and from network byte "
"order (MSB) byte arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:203
msgid ""
"The `fromByteArray()` method will take an array and create an appropriate"
" IPv4 or IPv6 object if the input satisfies the requirements. For IPv4 it"
" has to be an array of four 8-bit values, while for IPv6 it has to be an "
"array of sixteen 8-bit values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/ipaddr.js_README.md:220
msgid ""
"Both objects also offer a `toByteArray()` method, which returns an array "
"in network byte order (MSB)."
msgstr ""

